+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. A request without a key or
+with an unknown key gets 401 `unauthorized`; a known key whose role may not
+use the route gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: what a viewer may, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that is not a `GET` (allowed or not) writes an audit entry
+`{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`; `keyName` is `null` when no
+known key was sent. `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first.
+
